From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:48:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] BrainWaves: its pages on tag pages, and #/b/<id> links to a
 bookmark
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Settings → BrainWaves connects a BrainWaves (its address and an API token). Burrow's server
calls BrainWaves with the token (never sent to the browser), and a tag page shows the
BrainWaves pages with that tag, nested tags included, linking to them (#/p/<id>).
#/b/<id> opens a bookmark, so other apps can link straight to it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
